          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for to fall, then the Malayalam for to live."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ആരും",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആരും — āruṁ — \"nobody (with a negative verb)\". Malayalam negates a verb by joining ഇല്ല (illa) onto it: ആരും വന്നില്ല — āruṁ vannilla — \"Nobody came.\" To say something is not a thing, it uses അല്ല (alla): ഇത് എന്റെ വീട് അല്ല — itŭ enṟe vīṭŭ alla — \"This is not my house.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആരും (āruṁ) is native Dravidian: ārŭ, \"who\" (DEDR 5151, with Tamil yār), with -uṁ, \"even, any\": with a negative verb, \"not anyone\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
