          "title": "You'll want to know: ആരെങ്കിലും",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആരെങ്കിലും — āreṅkiluṁ — \"anyone, someone\". A yes-or-no question ends in -ഓ (-ō): ഉണ്ട് becomes ഉണ്ടോ. അവിടെ ആരെങ്കിലും ഉണ്ടോ? — aviṭe āreṅkiluṁ uṇṭō? — \"Is anyone there?\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആരെങ്കിലും (āreṅkiluṁ) is native Dravidian: ārŭ, \"who\" (DEDR 5151), then a conditional form meaning \"if\", from the verb \"to say\" (DEDR 868, with Tamil eṉ), and -uṁ: \"whoever it may be\"."
            }
          ]
        },
